steps.text:
I can't create work streams, so I sent the request to my manager, Cascade, and they will need to create it.

The request asks for a work stream titled "Migrate the docs site to Astro". It notes that Noah wants it done this quarter. The scope covers:
- auditing the current docs site;
- setting up an Astro project that matches the existing content and URLs, with redirects for any paths that change;
- updating the build, deploy and CI setup;
- checking that the new site matches the old one before cutover.

It also lists open questions for planning:
- which docs framework the site uses today;
- whether to use Astro Starlight;
- where the new site will be deployed;
- the exact deadline.

It asks Cascade to set up a dedicated worktree and branch off `main` and to pick a flow with review gates.

I haven't confirmed that Cascade has created the work stream yet.
